SDE-FLTK changes (Selviana DE Project)

1.4.5-sde1  2026-10-24
  - Imported FLTK 1.4.5 (tag release-1.4.5, upstream revision
    a9b1113516ffd15fc7602a6d425a317df30f4720) in place of FLTK 1.3.11, the
    way 1.3.11 was imported: without the test and example programs, the
    upstream CI files (.github, .gitlab-ci.yml, public/), the documentation
    sources (the man pages stay) and the bundled libraries (zlib, libjpeg and
    libpng; the system libraries are used). The bundled libdecor and nanosvg
    are left out too: SDE-FLTK is built for X11 only and without SVG images,
    so CMake/options.cmake defaults FLTK_BACKEND_WAYLAND and FLTK_OPTION_SVG
    to OFF. Drawing uses Xlib with Xft fonts as with 1.3 (no cairo or pango
    graphics driver): SDE programs draw with Xlib and cairo themselves.
  - X11: FLTK's GUI scaling is off (Fl_X11_Screen_Driver::rescalable()).
    SDE programs scale themselves with the SDE scale setting; FLTK 1.4 would
    scale them a second time from Xft.dpi, FLTK_SCALING_FACTOR, Ctrl+/-/0
    and later Xft.dpi changes. Every screen keeps the scale factor 1, so
    windows, fonts and coordinates are in pixels as with FLTK 1.3.
  - The SDE changes of 1.3.11-sde1 to -sde3, re-applied to the FLTK 1.4
    code: the FL/Fl_SDE_Style.H theme hooks (popup menus with the padded
    layout, icons and the quick-action row; Fl_Menu_Bar with hover,
    Fl_Choice, Fl_Scrollbar, Fl_Return_Button, tooltips; the fl_ask.H
    dialogs, now built by Fl_Message, and Fl_File_Chooser), styled menus
    kept inside the work area, X11 drag and drop serving text/uri-list and
    Fl_X::before_map (now declared in FL/platform.H). The Fl_Callback0/
    Fl_Callback1 cast change is not needed any more: FLTK 1.4 casts through
    void * and fl_intptr_t itself.
  - Fl_Menu_Bar: the menu bar under the pointer is a watched widget pointer
    (Fl::watch_widget_pointer), so a hovered menu bar that is deleted no
    longer leaves a dangling pointer behind.
  - fl_config.cmake.in: FLTK_USE_SVG is left undefined when SVG support is
    off (#cmakedefine, as in fl_config.in). Upstream's #cmakedefine01
    defined it as 0, the sources test it with #ifdef, and a build without
    SVG still compiled the SVG image code and needed the nanosvg headers.
  - X11: the "boxcheat" of FLTK 1.3 is back (disabled in FLTK 1.4): a
    single-buffered window with a filled box gets its color as the X
    background pixel, so a window that is mapped, exposed or enlarged shows
    that color instead of black or stale pixels until it is drawn.
  - X11 with an input method: a window that the program moves no longer
    sends FL_FOCUS again to a focused group (the window itself, say), which
    answered by giving the focus to its first child; the keyboard focus
    stays where it was, as with FLTK 1.3.
  - X11: the dotted keyboard focus box is the one of FLTK 1.3 again, a thin
    line around the same pixels (FLTK 1.4 drew a 1 pixel wide line, with the
    dots elsewhere, one pixel further right and down).
  - Menus: Up in a menu with nothing selected goes to the last item again,
    as with FLTK 1.3 (FLTK 1.4 did nothing; Up, Return picks the last item
    of a context menu, "App info..." in the Start menu, say).
  - fl_contrast() uses the FLTK 1.3 rule (FL_CONTRAST_LEGACY) by default:
    the SDE themes are made for it, and the CIELAB rule of FLTK 1.4 picks
    other text colors on some accents (selected text on the green and
    orange accents of Graphite light, for instance).

1.3.11-sde3  2026-10-24
  - X11: Fl_X::before_map, called right before a new top-level window is
    mapped for the first time, so programs can set _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE and
    _NET_WM_STATE before a window manager starts managing the window.
  - FL/Fl_Widget.H, FL/Fl_Menu_Item.H: the Fl_Callback0/Fl_Callback1
    setters cast through void (*)() so that programs built with -Wextra
    (GCC -Wcast-function-type) no longer get a warning per widget call.
    No change in behavior or ABI.
  - FL/Fl_SDE_Style.H declares Fl_Menu_Item as the struct it is (Clang
    -Wmismatched-tags in every program that includes it).

1.3.11-sde2  2026-10-21
  - FL/Fl_SDE_Style.H: theme hooks. With a style installed (fl_sde_style()),
    popup menus use a padded layout with variable item heights, icons and a
    row of quick actions (FL_MENU_SDE_QUICK items), and are drawn by the
    style; Fl_Menu_Bar (with hover), Fl_Choice, Fl_Scrollbar, Fl_Return_Button
    and the tooltip window ask the style first; fl_ask.H dialogs and
    Fl_File_Chooser are passed to the style before they are shown.
    Left/Right move along the quick row. Without a style nothing changes.
  - Menus that would leave the work area move into it (styled menus only).
  - X11 drag and drop: a file list that Fl::dnd() announces as
    "text/uri-list" is also served in that type, so GTK file managers
    accept files dragged from SDE programs (the desktop).

1.3.11-sde1  2026-10-20
  - Imported FLTK 1.3.11 into the SDE repository as SDE-FLTK.
  - Removed test/example programs, IDE files, documentation sources and the
    bundled zlib/libjpeg/libpng (system libraries are used).
  - FL/sde_fltk.h: SDE_FLTK_VERSION for SDE programs ("About" pages).
